flowchart TD
    %% Reliability flow: how every AI output (hint, win message, secret pick) is checked
    %% and replaced by a safe fallback, so the AI can never break the game.

    Need(["A feature needs text from Gemini"])
    Avail{"AI toggle ON and key present?"}
    Send["Send the prompt to Gemini (15 second timeout)"]
    Got{"What came back?"}
    Guard{"Guardrail check on the reply"}
    TriesLeft{"Second try still available?"}
    Use(["Show the AI text"])
    Fallback(["Fallback: static hint, plain win message or random.randint. Always correct, never blocks the game"])

    Truth["Ground truth is code, not the AI: check_guess decides Too High / Too Low / Win, update_score decides points. Gemini only writes the wording"]
    Guards["Guardrails. Hint: no secret number as digits or words, exactly one of higher / lower and it matches check_guess. Win message: contains the secret number and the final score. Secret pick: JSON integer inside the chosen band"]

    subgraph Verify["How the design is verified"]
        Pytest["pytest with a mocked Gemini: every guardrail rule, retry, fallback and rate-limit path. Deliberately broken code was caught"]
        Eval["tests/eval_hints.py: records every raw reply, then reports accuracy and leak rate before the guardrail and what was shown after it, plus API failures"]
    end

    Need --> Avail
    Avail -->|"no"| Fallback
    Avail -->|"yes"| Send
    Send --> Got
    Got -->|"429 rate limited"| Fallback
    Got -->|"timeout, empty reply or other error"| TriesLeft
    Got -->|"a reply"| Guard
    Guard -->|"pass"| Use
    Guard -->|"fail"| TriesLeft
    TriesLeft -->|"yes: retry once, telling Gemini why the last reply was rejected"| Send
    TriesLeft -->|"no"| Fallback

    Guard -.->|"rules"| Guards
    Truth -.->|"the guardrail compares against it"| Guard
    Pytest -.->|"covers"| Guard
    Eval -.->|"measures raw replies and shown text"| Guard
    Eval -.->|"counts"| Got

    %% Colours: green = the AI text is shown, amber = the plain version is used instead (explicit text colours so they read in light and dark mode)
    classDef good fill:#2e7d32,stroke:#1b5e20,stroke-width:2px,color:#ffffff
    classDef warn fill:#b26a00,stroke:#7a4a00,stroke-width:2px,color:#ffffff
    class Use good
    class Fallback warn
